Answer: Integer.MAX_VALUE represents the maximum value that can be stored in an int, while Integer.MIN_VALUE represents the minimum value.

```java
System.out.println(Integer.MAX_VALUE);
System.out.println(Integer.MIN_VALUE);
```

Output: 2147483647 -2147483648 They are predefined constants provided by the Integer class.
